**ABOUT INEVENT**
InEvent is an innovative and agile B2B startup that develops intelligent solutions for events and marketing for large enterprises, creating high-level management tools for executives and robust operational tools for analysts and managers.
**WHO WE ARE**
InEvent is a remote event technology company with InEventers in more than 13 different countries, speaking over 27 languages. We are a truly global team.
InEventers are a unique team with a growth mindset and shared values. We empower you to be yourself and encourage open communication. What matters most here is not your past experience, but your curiosity and passion to learn and grow with us!
**QUALITY ANALYST**
InEvent is looking for a detail-oriented, problem-solving Quality Analyst who will play a critical role in optimizing the development of our products. You will be responsible for ensuring that we deliver high-quality, flawlessly functioning software and applications.
**RESPONSIBILITIES**
• Develop testing systems for our public API and simulate use cases for our applications;
• Identify, fix, and resolve issues and security vulnerabilities found during testing;
• Analyze test results and report findings to the development team;
• Work closely with the development team to fix bugs and errors;
• Learn the development models used across our platforms;
• Innovate and restructure parts of our systems.
**IDEAL PROFILE**
• At least 6 months of experience testing web platforms;
• Degree completed or in progress in Systems Analysis and Development or a related field;
• Good working knowledge of test management software, programming languages, and QA methodologies;
• Strong teamwork and critical thinking skills;
• Ability to learn quickly and identify effective problem-solving approaches;
• Creativity and curiosity to learn and apply new concepts to our platforms;
• Enjoys hackathons and has a hacker mindset—when challenged, solves problems with passion and drive. |
**BENEFITS**
• Paid Time Off (PTO);
• Global health insurance;
• Language learning programs;
• Lunch days and other monthly activities;
• Regular evening Happy Hours and Breakfast Club with teammates;
• Monthly/quarterly challenges and games with prizes;
• Birthday gifts and work anniversary gifts.
**CONTRACT**
This is a permanent, full-time position (40 hours per week) under an independent contractor agreement.
If you believe this role is for you, bring your personal notebook (Mac or Windows) and a mobile device (iOS or Android) and come work with us!
